{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793277763,"nonce":"w5zMDVT5DNIS8oRA7+tukIppJXw=","title":"Every resource should belong to one org, and an org admin should see and act only inside that org, the way Claude Teams and organizations work. ForgeConnections do not today.","message":"What is server-wide today:\n- `ForgeConnection` is `{id, kind, base_url, credential_ref}` with no org (`crates/scarab-forge/src/lib.rs:765`, migration `0023`).\n- The connection routes (list, add, preflight, bind repos, resync) only call `authorize_org_administer`, which passes for an admin of any org (`crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:8985`).\n- Every GitHub App installation connection shares `credential_ref \"github-app\"` (`lib.rs:6119`), and App mode mints a token for whichever repo is named. An admin of org `globex` can bind, preflight or read a repo of org `acme` if the App can see it.\n- There is no orgs table: an org exists as the `org` column of a repo binding (`administrable_orgs`, `lib.rs:3170-3200`).\n\nFound while building ADR-0076 step 2 (installing private libraries through a connection). Step 2 works around it: a private install is allowed only when the source repo's owner is the org or the repo is bound to that org (owner decision 2026-10-29, option A).\n\nWanted:\n- An org record, and every org-owned resource (connections, repo bindings, environments, secrets, policies, plugin installations, library installations, API tokens) keyed by it.\n- Connection routes authorize against the connection's org, not \"admin of some org\".\n- A GitHub App connection belongs to the org of the installation's account; a token is minted only for repos of that installation.\n- Audit the rest of the API for other server-wide resources reachable by any org admin.\n- Expand/contract migration; existing connections assigned to the org(s) of their current bindings.","files":null}]}